From: OpenGrad <https://github.com/arrogance231/OpenGrad>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] backends/qualcomm: skip higher-order ops in LiftConstantScalarOperands

`LiftConstantScalarOperands._create_tensor_args` dereferences `node.target._schema` for every
`call_function` node in the graph. That holds for ATen ops, but a `HigherOrderOperator` has no
`_schema`, so the pass raises:

    AttributeError: 'AutoFunctionalizedV2' object has no attribute '_schema'

`auto_functionalized_v2` is PyTorch's functionalization wrapper for ops that mutate their inputs,
so this fires for any model that mutates state in place. It was hit exporting Qwen3.5-2B, whose
Gated DeltaNet layers update their recurrent state in place
(`examples/models/llama/attention.py::_recurrent_gated_delta_rule`).

A higher-order op has no constant scalar operands for this pass to lift, so skipping it is the
correct behaviour rather than a workaround.

Applies to: pytorch/executorch @ df6147afadf106a0ef3a74f65d80b5c589e63e44

---
 backends/qualcomm/_passes/lift_constant_scalar_operands.py | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/backends/qualcomm/_passes/lift_constant_scalar_operands.py b/backends/qualcomm/_passes/lift_constant_scalar_operands.py
--- a/backends/qualcomm/_passes/lift_constant_scalar_operands.py
+++ b/backends/qualcomm/_passes/lift_constant_scalar_operands.py
@@ -182,6 +182,12 @@ class LiftConstantScalarOperands(ExportPass):
     def _lift(self, gm: torch.fx.GraphModule) -> None:
         for n in gm.graph.nodes:
             if (
                 n.op != "call_function"
                 or isinstance(n.target, (BuiltinMethodType, BuiltinFunctionType))
                 or n.target in SKIP_LIFT_OPS
+                # Higher-order ops (auto_functionalized_v2, wrapping in-place state mutation
+                # such as Qwen3.5's Gated DeltaNet recurrent state) carry no `_schema`, and
+                # _create_tensor_args dereferences it unconditionally. A HOP has no liftable
+                # constant scalar operands anyway, so skipping is correct.
+                or not hasattr(n.target, "_schema")
             ):
                 continue

             if tensor_args := self._create_tensor_args(n, gm):
                 self._update_node(n, tensor_args)
